-- title:
--   Local principality of the closure divisor along the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $X=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ (the pushout of the charts with $j$, resp. $j^{-1}$, adjoined). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$, $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, together with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ into the base change $X\times_A k$ over $k$, whose images cover $X\times_A k$, with $C_1\times_{X} C_2$ reduced and of cardinality $n>0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O:A\to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa:O\to k$ a surjection with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ the structure map $A\to k$; let $bc:X\times_A k\to X\times_A O$ be the induced morphism, compatible with the projection to $X$ and with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ on the base. Assume the ideal sheaves $\ker(i_1\ {\rm followed\ by}\ bc)$ and $\ker(i_2\ {\rm followed\ by}\ bc)$ are invertible (locally, on an affine basic open, generated by one non-zero-divisor) and that their product is $\ker bc$. Let $T'$ be a fraction field of $O$, assume the generic fibre $X\times_A T'\to\operatorname{Spec}T'$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, let $E$ be a relative effective Cartier divisor of degree $r$ on $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}T'$ and $\bar E$ one over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ (in each case an ideal sheaf whose closed subscheme is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over the base with fibre rank $r$ everywhere), such that $\bar E$'s ideal is the kernel of the closed immersion of $E$'s subscheme followed by the map $X\times_A T'\to X\times_A O$, and such that $\bar E$ is $\varpi$-saturated for every irreducible $\varpi\in O$: on each affine open $U$ of $X\times_A O$, if the restriction of the pullback of $\varpi$ times a section $s$ lies in $\bar E$'s ideal on $U$, then so does $s$. The conclusion is that for every point $z$ of $X\times_A k$ there are an affine open $U$ of $X\times_A O$ containing $bc(z)$ and a section $g\in\bar E.I(U)$ whose image generates the extension of $\bar E.I(U)$ to the localisation of $\Gamma(U)$ at the prime of $bc(z)$, and whose image there is a non-zero-divisor.
--
--   This is the special-fibre half of the assertion that the saturated schematic closure of a relative effective Cartier divisor on the generic fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ is again an effective Cartier divisor: at the points coming from the reducible mod-$p$ fibre $C_1\cup C_2$ the ideal of the closure is principal in the local ring, generated by a non-zero-divisor. It feeds the construction of the closure as a relative effective Cartier divisor over $O$ with invertible comap ideal, used in the study of the Jacobian of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
